error[E0277]: this subscriber has no native pages to cap
  --> tests/ui/subscriber_batch_without_pages.rs:19:26
   |
19 |     let _capped = handle.batch(nonzero!(64));
   |                          ^^^^^ `batch(..)` caps the pages a page body is handed
   |
   = help: the trait `ruststream::runtime::CapsPages` is not implemented for `HandleValue<Solo<Order>, (), (), (), handle, ruststream::runtime::Probed>`
   = note: the cap applies to a page body that settles its own page (`&[T]`, `&[F<'_>]`, `&[Message<H, P>]`, returning outcomes); a single-message body has no page, and a page that replies or publishes through an `Out` slot settles as a whole. To batch single deliveries on the client instead, name the framework's buffer with `buffered(max, wait)`
